From c5505e2c47a7046846852c25ac50690291533091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:59:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] drm/panfrost: Don't WARN when a GEM mapping cannot get
 its pages

Running out of memory at a memory cgroup limit is an ordinary error
here, which userspace gets. Drop the WARN_ON() that adds a backtrace.

Fixes: f3ba91228e8e ("drm/panfrost: Add initial panfrost driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
index 6cd1678..2e43b37 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@ int panfrost_mmu_map(struct panfrost_gem_mapping *mapping)
 		prot |= IOMMU_NOEXEC;
 
 	sgt = drm_gem_shmem_get_pages_sgt(shmem);
-	if (WARN_ON(IS_ERR(sgt)))
+	if (IS_ERR(sgt))
 		return PTR_ERR(sgt);
 
 	ret = mmu_map_sg(pfdev, mapping->mmu, mapping->mmnode.start << PAGE_SHIFT,
-- 
2.55.0

